FIX.log - lab fixes and validation, 2026-11-05
==============================================

Scope: make WORKSHOP.md Steps 6-10 show a clear Before -> After for their
primitive. Validated with GitHub Copilot CLI 1.0.105 (default model), each run
in a temporary clone of main with the earlier examples/stepNN-* folders copied
in order. Not validated: VS Code, Claude Code (login expired), Codex.

Changes on main
---------------

1. fix(lab): step10 guard blocks agents ending the red phase  (5e7e541)
   Problem: tdd-red ran `touch .tdd-red`, then `rm .tdd-red` itself (the prompt
   says "then make it pass") and edited src/. The hook only checked edit tools,
   so it only *asked*, like the instructions. Before and After both edited
   src/ in 1 of 2 runs.
   Change:
   - examples/step10-hooks/scripts/hooks/guard-edits.sh: while .tdd-red exists,
     deny shell commands (rm/unlink/mv/git ... .tdd-red) that remove it.
   - examples/step10-hooks/scripts/hooks/lib.sh: new shell_command helper;
     strip_root removes every spelling of the repo root (git root, physical
     path, $PWD, payload cwd). Before, a symlinked path (/tmp vs /private/tmp)
     failed open and infra/ edits were allowed.
   - tdd-red.md / tdd-green.md: the user removes .tdd-red before tdd-green.
   - Claude and Codex PreToolUse matchers (step10 and step11, plus the step11
     plugin hooks.json) now include Bash so shell calls reach the guard.
   - WORKSHOP.md Step 10 Read/After; docs/agent-compatibility.md: Copilot CLI
     loads repo hooks only in trusted folders.
   Result (Copilot CLI):
   - tdd-red prompt: Before edited src/ in 2 of 3 runs; After 2/2 denied
     "Red phase: only the user can end it", agent stopped, src/ untouched.
   - infra prompt: Before 3/3 edited infra/main.bicep; After denied
     "Edits under infra/ need a human".
   - syntax error: After, post-edit hook reported CS1513.
   - 13 direct hook payload cases pass (Copilot CLI, VS Code, Claude, Codex shapes).

2. docs(lab): known issues and workarounds in WORKSHOP.md, this FIX.log
   WORKSHOP.md gains a "Known issues" table plus notes in Steps 7 and 8.

3. fix(lab): step10 asks before infra/ edits instead of denying
   Problem (seen live): the infra deny reason said "Ask the user first". The
   agent asked in chat, the user approved, and the hook denied again: hooks
   are stateless and a deny cannot be approved.
   Change: lib.sh gains emit_ask (permissionDecision "ask"); guard-edits.sh
   uses it for infra/. Red-phase checks run first and stay deny. Codex falls
   back to deny (no verified "ask" support, so it never allows silently).
   WORKSHOP.md Step 10 teaches deny vs ask; agent-compatibility.md notes it.
   Result (Copilot CLI 1.0.105):
   - interactive: "Hook permission request ... Do you want to allow this tool
     call?" appeared even with --allow-all; approving applied the edit.
   - copilot -p: "Denied, no one to approve" (fails closed).
   - direct payloads: copilot/claude infra -> ask; codex infra -> deny;
     red phase src/infra/rm marker -> deny; red phase tests -> allow.

