Known issues (also in WORKSHOP.md "Known issues")
-------------------------------------------------

- Step 2 rules leak later answers: docs/rules/blazor.md has `@key="task.Id"`
  (Step 7 fix) and "Debounce search inputs" (part of the Step 8 fix). Not
  changed because Step 2 is parked and its checklist uses those rules.
  Workaround: score Step 7 on browser reproduction, Step 8 on numbers.
- Step 2 Before scores 3/4 without rules (parked, see handoff).
- User-level skills/plugins/MCP contaminate Before runs (seen: ~/.agents/skills/tdd
  took over tdd-red; an agent-browser plugin and chrome-devtools MCP gave Before a
  browser). Workaround: disable them, or check the session log.
- Repo skills lab-inspect-session and lab-score-run (facilitator tools) are
  visible to attendee agents. Harmless for the step prompts.
- Copilot CLI: repo hooks/skills/MCP need a trusted folder (no warning);
  `--trust-folder` cannot be combined with `--resume`.
- find-pid.sh takes the first CRUDTasksWithAgent process; run one app copy only.

How to re-run the validation
----------------------------

  git clone --branch main <repo> /tmp/labN && cd /tmp/labN
  for s in step01 step02 ... stepNN; do cp -R examples/$s*/. ./; git add -A; git commit -qm "lab: $s copy example"; done
  copilot --trust-folder --allow-all -p "<exact prompt from WORKSHOP.md>" [--agent <name>]
  git status --short   # score against the step checklist
